WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.230
<b>Kingdom</b>

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:33.230
Myra!

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.700
Three each of the knight's 
stew and brown bread.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.860
Sure. Coming right up!

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:41.990
Two of those over here, too. With extra meat.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.870
You got it!

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.480
Dad, five more knight's stews.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.090
Extra meat in two of them.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:54.240
Got it.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:01:59.890
Here are the extra meat ones first.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:01.240
Thanks.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:05.890
Thank you for waiting. 
Here's your knight's stew.

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:07.140
Enjoy.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:10.100
I've been looking forward to eating this!

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:12.520
Thank you very much!

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.480
Great meal.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:18.870
That's exact change. Please come again!

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:21.580
It's finally calmed down a bit.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.620
I'm exhausted.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.400
I'll handle the rest.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.620
You can take a break until the evening shift.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.880
I'm so tired.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:40.560
<i>After Dad learned how to make knight's stew,</i>

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:43.880
<i>our lifestyle turned around.</i>

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.640
What? Knight's stew?

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.970
Yeah.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:50.120
I just offered them 100 silver,

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.400
and they happily taught me how to make it.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.150
What did you just say?

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:56.740
I offered them 100 silver—

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:59.750
A hundred silvers?! 
That's half a month's earnings!

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:03.520
You know we can't afford that, don't you?!

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:08.390
I'm sorry I didn't talk 
to you about it first.

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:09.310
But...

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:12.030
It'll be fine! Don't worry!

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:15.540
We can make 100 silver coins back in no time!

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.960
Did you see how those people 
reacted after eating it?

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:21.300
It's gonna become our signature dish!

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:25.730
<i>A hundred silvers...</i>

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.730
<i>In the end, Dad's judgment 
proved to be right.</i>

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:36.910
<i>Knight's stew became so popular, it earned
 us 100 silver coins in five days.</i>

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:43.560
Being so busy is a good thing, but still...

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.740
Maybe I'll sleep for a bit.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:50.140
Just a little nap, like I used 
to when we had spare time...

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.380
Hey, Myra!

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:02.930
Darn it... Just when I was 
about to fall asleep.

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:07.510
Hi!

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:09.690
Johan... What is it?

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:11.910
Huh? Wait, are you angry?

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:13.550
Did I do something wrong?

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.350
Not at all.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.100
Okay, good!

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.530
I found this incredible restaurant. 
Want to go there with me?

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:26.160
An incredible restaurant? Is there 
a place like that in our town?

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:30.000
I found it a while back. 
It's kind of... different.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.890
The food is unbelievably good!

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:33.920
Unbelievably?

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:37.290
Well, I can go if we'll be back by evening.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:40.550
Yeah, that's the spirit! C'mon, let's hurry!

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:44.800
Okay, I guess that's settled. Let's go!

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:57.590
Hey, Johan...

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:00.820
Are you pulling some kind of trick on me?

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.930
Why did you invite me out to eat,

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:05.920
and then lead me into the forest?

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:11.290
I heard wolves are seen in 
this forest sometimes, too.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:12.990
I'm not tricking you!

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:15.860
This is the way to the incredible restaurant.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:19.840
And if any wolves show up, I'll protect you.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:21.770
Well, that worries me.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:26.340
What does that mean? I am part 
of the town watch, you know!

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:28.530
I know.

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:32.520
So how did you find out that 
there was a restaurant out here?

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:36.850
Oh, well, remember when that married 
halfling chef couple passed through?

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:38.770
With the knight's stew?

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:40.580
Exactly.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:42.940
Apparently, they went off into this forest,

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:45.130
singing some weird song.

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:50.160
I figured there must be 
something in this forest,

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.310
so I came to look a few times.

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:53.370
Uh-huh.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.330
And I found that.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:05.760
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.670
What's a door doing in 
the middle of the forest?

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:10.610
That's where we're headed.

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:11.760
It's Nekoya.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:16.770
Welcome!

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:23.020
H-Horns?!

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:26.030
Oh, um... I'm actually a demon.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:30.240
Wow... I've never met a demon before.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.930
I thought they looked kind of,
 well... intimidating,

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:35.040
but I guess some of them are cute, too!

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.480
C-Cu—

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:38.640
W-Well, thank you!

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:40.790
Help yourselves to any open seats.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.290
We appreciate it.

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:46.300
Here are your complimentary glasses 
of water and wet hand towels.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:49.480
Let me know when you're ready to order.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:01.600
What an unusual shop.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:05.610
The outfit that worker girl 
is wearing seems so... short.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:08.440
Apparently, that's normal in the other world.

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:09.540
Huh...

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:12.170
Wait, did you just say "other world"?

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:13.570
This is another world?!

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:16.240
Oh, I didn't tell you?

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:18.700
No, you did not!

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:20.390
Sorry about that.

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:24.660
But there's no doubt that the food is good!

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:26.460
Let's decide what to eat.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:31.810
Wow, they have a lot to choose from.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:35.500
The prices are just a bit higher than ours.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:39.650
That's true, but when you order food here,

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:43.000
it comes with all the bread 
and soup you can eat!

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:43.800
What?!

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:48.400
And the bread is such a fine white bread 
that you could get a whole gold coin for it!

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.400
And you get all you can eat?!

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:52.400
And I recommend...

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:53.950
Let's see...

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:54.910
This one.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:56.660
Macaroni gratin?

00:07:56.660 --> 00:08:00.410
Yeah. It's just like 
knight's stew, but even better!

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:03.710
It's made with knight's sauce, 
topped with cheese, and baked...

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:06.620
Okay, let's get this.

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:07.650
All right, great!

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:08.800
We're ready!

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:10.170
Coming!

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:13.550
Macaroni gratin with bread, two orders.

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:16.780
Coming right up. Please wait just a bit.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:22.600
<i>Macaroni Gratin</i>

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:22.600
Thank you for waiting.
Here is your macaroni gratin.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:25.890
It is quite hot, so please 
eat it with caution.

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:27.850
Yes! I've been waiting for this!

00:08:27.850 --> 00:08:30.010
Please enjoy.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:33.530
So this is macaroni gratin?

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:40.290
<i>The knight's sauce and 
cheese both smell so good.</i>

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:44.710
This is the stuff!

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:49.630
<i>Hot, hot, hot!</i>

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:54.220
There you go.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:03.340
It's hot, but it's so good!

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:06.340
Go on, Myra, eat yours before it gets cold.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:09.480
It's really good!

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:10.920
R-Right.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:15.270
<i>It does look hot, so I'll 
start with the bread.</i>

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:23.500
<i>It's delicious!</i>

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:27.410
<i>The outside is crispy, 
but the inside is soft and moist.</i>

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:32.250
And this delicious bread is all-you-can-eat?

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:37.880
This other world's pretty amazing, huh?

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:40.890
It really is!

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:47.140
The bread's good, too, but you 
gotta try the macaroni gratin now!

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:48.520
All right.

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:53.470
Hot!

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:05.490
<i>The charred cheese fills my 
mouth with its savory aroma.</i>

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:07.820
<i>It's giving me even more of an appetite!</i>

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:13.170
<i>Inside it is... oranie, 
chicken, mushrooms, and...</i>

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:15.160
<i>Noodles?</i>

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:20.680
<i>What a strange shape. 
There's a hole through it.</i>

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:27.530
<i>When I bite into it, the sauce 
packed into the hole bursts out!</i>

00:10:27.530 --> 00:10:30.200
<i>The rich flavor of milk in the knight's sauce</i>

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:33.640
<i>and the sourness of the 
cheese enhance one another!</i>

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:35.440
Delicious!

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:40.550
If...

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:44.320
If you could eat this at our shop,
 what would you think?

00:10:45.590 --> 00:10:49.080
If I could eat this at your place,
 I'd go there every day!

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:50.740
Really?

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:55.200
Well, if you say so, 
maybe I should try to make it!

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:56.620
Great!

00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:59.010
If you need a taste-tester, 
I'll be there anytime!

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:00.550
I will charge you, of course.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.440
Aw, c'mon!

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.380
Quick, before it gets cold.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:13.440
<b>Duchy</b>

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.830
I haven't seen the sea in so long.

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:22.950
It's still so big.

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:25.950
You've been here before, Far?

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:28.950
Yes, about 50 years ago.

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:34.240
We finally made it to the sea.

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:40.720
<i>I've been traveling with 
Alice ever since then.</i>

00:11:46.690 --> 00:11:49.170
We've been through a lot, but now...

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:53.580
Okay, Alice, let's look for some sea 
grasses we can use as seasoning.

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:56.250
Huh? Are you kidding me?!

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:58.480
Where did you go, Alice?!

00:11:58.710 --> 00:12:00.490
Alice!

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:05.490
Come one, come all!

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:09.950
I've got rare kaffa brought in 
from all the way across the sea!

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:07.900
Where are you, Alice?

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:14.590
Rumor has it the emperor himself 
over in the empire loves it!

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:16.960
How 'bout it? Wanna sample a taste?

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.080
Do you have white sugar?

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:22.540
I've been getting a lot of orders 
from the Shrine of Light lately,

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:24.300
so I'd like to stock up.

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:26.430
What's the deal with these prices?

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:29.450
I could get five of the finest bottles 
of the Land of Sea's plum wine

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:30.970
for the cost of one bottle here!

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:32.470
Don't you know?

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:35.190
This is the newest dwarven firewater!

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.090
You there, young lady!

00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:39.190
Care for a croquette fresh out of the fryer?

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:43.700
<i>Last time I came here, 
it was practically deserted.</i>

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:48.700
<i>Can human towns change this 
much in just 50 years?</i>

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.640
I've lived in quiet forests all my life.

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:54.650
I don't do well in noisy places like this.

00:12:57.550 --> 00:12:58.630
There she is!

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:03.460
Alice!

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:07.390
Don't I always tell you not 
to wander around on your own?

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:09.890
I'm sorry.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:12.720
Honestly... Be more careful, all right?

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:14.620
Anyway, what were you looking at?

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:15.580
This.

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:23.280
It looks like slime. Is this food?

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:27.160
Well, yes. It's a dessert called fruit jelly.

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:29.530
Fruit jelly...

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:31.540
Feel free to try some.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:34.760
I served some to another 
elf like you a while back,

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:36.860
and she said it was delicious.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:41.160
Okay. We'll take two, then.

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:42.300
Yeah!

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:44.000
Thanks for your business!

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:45.900
Here you go.

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:47.800
Thank you.

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:52.800
Wow, this is pretty good.

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:55.600
This slippery texture is fascinating.

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:57.810
Yeah! This is really good!

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:03.980
<i>I guess there are people in this 
world who make things like this, too.</i>

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:11.070
Is this made by boiling fruit in sugar and 
water, and letting the juice solidify?

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:16.580
<i>But how do they make the 
juice solidify like this?</i>

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:18.300
Excuse me.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:21.080
How do you make this?

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:23.470
I don't know, actually.

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:25.150
If you want to know how it's made,

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:28.220
you should visit the witch 
who lives on the cape.

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:30.470
Thank you.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:32.510
Will this cover the cost?

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:36.780
Come on, Alice, let's go.

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:54.210
Lord of Blue, who reigns over the water,

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:55.810
grant me your blessing.

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:59.400
Grant me legs to walk upon the land.

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:14.600
I gathered quite a few.

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:24.930
Now, what shall I make with these today?

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:29.370
A visitor? How unusual.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:36.240
Um... Who might you be?

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:39.940
I am Fardania, and this is Alice.

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:44.170
We heard about you from 
a merchant in the market.

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:48.250
I was told that you make the fruit 
jelly they sell in the market.

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:49.480
Is that true?

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:51.630
Yes, that's right.

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:55.220
Would you teach me how 
to make your fruit jelly?

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:57.140
It was incredibly delicious.

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:03.570
I'm sorry. I meant no harm.

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:07.210
Please, come in. 
I'll teach you how to make it.

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:16.160
Did you gather these plants from the sea?

00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:18.410
Yes, I did.

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:22.480
Do you use them to season 
your cooking, by any chance?

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:23.880
I do indeed.

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:28.880
Would you like to have some of them?

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:31.840
Can I?! Yes, I'd love some!

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:34.010
Then I'll send them with you when you leave.

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:35.190
Thank you!

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:37.760
Please, have a drink.

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:39.850
Thank you!

00:16:41.090 --> 00:16:41.560
Ah, hot!

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:43.180
Are you okay?

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:44.260
Yeah...

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:48.300
Now, you wanted to know how 
to make fruit jelly, yes?

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:49.230
Yes.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:56.190
I must tell you one thing first.

00:16:56.190 --> 00:17:00.100
The fruit jelly I make is 
not the finished product.

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:01.870
Is that all right with you?

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:04.120
That's not even finished?

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:07.410
No, the real product is even softer.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:10.900
I don't mind if it's unfinished.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:12.740
That's good to hear.

00:17:13.520 --> 00:17:15.710
Um, may I ask you a question?

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:16.890
Of course.

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:20.760
What gave you the idea to solidify 
it into such a slime-like state?

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:24.270
No other meals or sweets would 
have given me that idea.

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:29.020
Oh, that wasn't my idea.

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:29.930
Huh?

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:34.500
I didn't come up with the 
idea for fruit jelly.

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:36.420
It was served at a certain shop,

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:39.280
and I tried reproducing it 
based on what I had seen.

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:40.930
A certain... shop?

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:47.010
What will I find today?

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:53.460
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:56.760
What could this be?

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:01.950
It's been 55 years since 
I started living here,

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:05.090
and I've never seen 
anything like this before.

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:09.310
I sense mana.

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:11.720
It's a form of teleportation magic.

00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:14.780
I wonder where it leads.

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:25.410
Welcome.

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:27.420
Um, what is...

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:31.330
Oh, is this your first time here?

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:35.670
This is a restaurant called 
Nekoya in another world.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:38.170
Another world? Restaurant?

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:39.870
Well, yes.

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:42.300
Would you care to eat 
something before you go?

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:44.560
All right, since you offered...

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:46.930
You can take any open seat.

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:53.090
Can you read the Eastern 
Continent's language?

00:18:53.090 --> 00:18:54.100
Yes.

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:55.940
This is our menu.

00:18:57.050 --> 00:19:00.740
And here's your complimentary 
glass of water and wet hand towel.

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.570
Complimentary?

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:05.580
Yes. That means they're free of charge.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:09.080
You can get refills, too, so ask
 any time if you need more.

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:13.890
<i>They have so many different foods.</i>

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:16.330
<i>But I just ate a meal,</i>

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:17.960
<i>so I should have something light.</i>

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:20.490
"Fruit jelly"?

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:24.690
"Fruits boiled with sugar and 
enveloped in a transparent slime."

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:27.970
They eat slime in this other world?

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:29.480
How curious.

00:19:29.990 --> 00:19:31.480
I'd like to order.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:32.480
Sure.

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:35.980
I'll have this thing you 
call "fruit jelly," please.

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:39.480
Fruit jelly? Please wait just a moment.

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:45.490
<i>Fruit Jelly</i>

00:19:41.350 --> 00:19:44.070
Thank you for waiting. 
Here's your fruit jelly.

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:45.490
Please enjoy.

00:19:46.180 --> 00:19:47.460
<i>How pretty.</i>

00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:52.340
<i>It's like I'm looking up at the 
water's surface from beneath it.</i>

00:19:52.340 --> 00:19:54.230
<i>The menu called it "slime,"</i>

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:56.000
<i>but I guess it was just metaphorical.</i>

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:06.160
<i>It feels so smooth on my tongue,</i>

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:08.910
<i>and then it melts right away.</i>

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:12.640
<i>A refreshing hint of sourness, 
and a light, clear sweetness...</i>

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:14.150
It tastes lovely!

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:18.770
<i>Is this mikele?</i>

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:21.200
<i>It's so sweet!</i>

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:23.990
<i>Compared to the mikeles I usually eat,</i>

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:26.450
<i>its sourness is milder and more palatable.</i>

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:28.990
<i>Ripe, sweet margos,</i>

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:31.740
<i>moskets that shine like jewels,</i>

00:20:31.740 --> 00:20:34.100
<i>tao fruits cut into crescents,</i>

00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:37.670
<i>and this yellow fruit that shreds 
lengthwise in my mouth...</i>

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:39.840
<i>What a luxurious dish!</i>

00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:45.050
<i>Each of the fruits is sweeter and more 
delicious than any I've ever eaten.</i>

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:49.300
<i>Is this what happens when 
they're boiled in sugar water?</i>

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:51.370
<i>I could eat this every day!</i>

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:53.790
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:57.980
<i>there is a kind of seaweed that 
can turn liquids into solids.</i>

00:20:57.980 --> 00:21:01.830
<i>Maybe I could make this fruit jelly.</i>

00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:04.640
<i>I'll try it when I get home.</i>

00:21:06.670 --> 00:21:09.990
I started making it after that.

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:15.120
But I haven't been able to replicate the 
softness of the jelly at Nekoya yet.

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:19.270
The jelly I make always 
seems to harden too much.

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:21.630
What is it?

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:24.130
Nekoya...

00:21:24.550 --> 00:21:28.510
Hey, Far! Isn't Nekoya the place 
where we had the rice burgers?

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:30.440
Yes, it is.

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:31.560
You know of it?

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:36.270
Nekoya is the reason Far started her journey.

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:38.400
Oh, is that right?

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:40.600
They got me again.

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:44.340
I can't bear to keep 
losing to them like this!

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:45.570
Miss Camilla!

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:46.540
Yes?

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:49.820
Let's make something even better 
than Nekoya's fruit jelly!

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:52.950
Good idea.

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:55.860
If I can borrow the knowledge 
you've gained in your travels,

00:21:55.860 --> 00:21:57.960
perhaps we can surpass it.

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:02.920
Shall we get started making 
something right away?

00:22:03.660 --> 00:22:04.920
Yes!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:42.560
<i>Teriyaki Burger</i>

00:23:42.560 --> 00:23:50.250
<i>Chocolate Parfait Again</i>
